6:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":"Avidya is not simply lack of data; it is existential mis-knowing. It is the root confusion by which the eternal Self is mistaken for body, mind, role, and story. From Avidya arise fear, attachment, egoism, and the entire structure of bondage. In both Yoga and Vedanta, liberation is impossible until this fundamental ignorance is weakened and dissolved."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"italic border-l-2 border-primary/20 pl-6 py-2","children":"Avidya is a foundational obstacle in the Yoga Sutras and a core explanatory principle in Vedanta. It explains why beings remain trapped in Samsara despite their essential spiritual nature."}]]}]
